cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FLARE, please cite the paper below."
title: "FLARE: a relational boundary engine for LLMs"
abstract: >-
  A small, auditable middleware layer that sits between an application and a
  language model, enforcing relational boundaries: no synthetic solidarity
  ("fake we"), no identity fusion, and no unbounded reassurance loops. Since
  v0.2 FLARE also evidences its own enforcement actions to an append-only
  audit stream, with heartbeats per active rule, so an external monitor can
  verify that a boundary held without ever reading what was said. The stream
  carries counts and outcomes only — never message text, never a user
  identifier.
